;; flint's own pod registry (`DECISIONS.md#pods-are-a-resolvable-dependency`).
;;
;; THIS ONE IS FOR flint's TOOLING and nothing else. It lists the pods that
;; live in this repository -- the dependency drivers, and whatever else sheds
;; out of the binary -- so flint's own build does not depend on third-party
;; infrastructure being up.
;;
;; It is NOT where a user's dependencies resolve from. Those resolve against
;; the community registry (`flint.deps.registry/community-registry`), because a
;; first-party registry that also answered for somebody else's coordinate would
;; quietly change what that coordinate means. A project that WANTS these pods
;; says so:
;;
;;     {:flint/pod-registries ["registry/pods.edn"]}
;;
;; ## The format
;;
;; A pod, its versions, and which artifact matches which host. Prebuilt per
;; platform is what a pod IS -- the host starts a program -- so an entry names
;; artifacts and not a way to build one. An artifact with neither `:os/name`
;; nor `:os/arch` matches anything; one marked `:artifact/wasm true` is the
;; FALLBACK, used only where no native artifact matches, so the matrix does not
;; have to be complete.
;;
;;     {:pods {pod.name {"1.2.0" {:pod/artifacts
;;                                [{:os/name "macos" :os/arch "aarch64"
;;                                  :artifact/url "https://.../pod-macos-aarch64.tgz"
;;                                  :artifact/sha256 "..."
;;                                  :artifact/executable "pod"}
;;                                 {:artifact/wasm true
;;                                  :artifact/url "https://.../pod.wasm"
;;                                  :artifact/executable "pod.wasm"}]}}}}
;;
;; ## Why it is empty
;;
;; Nothing has moved out of the binary yet. The npm, maven and git drivers are
;; still compiled in (`cli/src/deps.rs`), and a registry entry for a pod that
;; does not exist would be a published lie. The entries land here as the
;; drivers are built and released; what exists now is the format and the hook
;; that reads it, which is what the fetching side needed in order to be
;; testable at all.
{:registry/name "flint tooling pods"
 :registry/scope :tooling
 :pods {}}
